nd this is the safest way to do it  right now  even maintaining a bank account can be  expensive for cannabis businesses  for a typical cannabis operator the cost  for maintaining a bank account can scale  up to about ten thousand dollars a month  nick friedman is cfo of theory wellness  a massachusetts-based company that also  operates in maine  starting theory we didn't have a huge  amount of capital at the time and we  purposely decided to keep it private and  not go  to private equity simply looking to our  own resources  and to friends and family to find the  funds to start the business  we raised about three million dollars  the industry has become much more  sophisticated  we're seeing it now taking hundreds of  thousands if not millions of dollars  to get operational if you only have one  place you can go for  loans or investment capital then they  have the ability to set the terms which  means you're much less likely to get  favorable weight we know businesses that  are paying  20 30 40 interest rates on business  loans  as the cost of participating in this  space has gone up  it has meant that poor and minority  communities  have faced much more of a challenge  trying to get a seed at the table  the challenge with it is you end up  giving  a pretty good chunk of your company away  in order to get your company financed  in massachusetts to open canada  provisions we raised five million  dollars  i would have wished we could have at  least gotten mortgages for our  properties because that would have been  probably a million and a half that i  wouldn't have had to raise  we would expect some pretty  consequential changes to the industry  landscape if federal  banking reform or something equivalent  to it were to pass  the first thing we would expect to see  is the significant drop  in the cost of financing the business  and as a result  we would expect to see a lot more  entrepreneurs start exploring  opportunities  in the space  i think one implication would simply be  the refinancing of some of our debt  which is  at interest rates that i would say is  less reflective of the risk state of our  business but simply more reflective of  the  limited supply of capital that exists  out there thank you  we still have to borrow at interest  rates that are extremely high  we are doing very well and any bank  that i went to with our numbers and our  balance sheet and our p  l would say how much do you want and how  quickly can i give it to you  i can't do that right now you should be  able to build on your success not only  as a company but also with your bank and  financial institutions to make sure that  you can keep growing as fast as the  market needs you to  and i think that's a big hindrance to us

